<section>
  <div class="wrap with-aside">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Ride wild. Live well.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Imagine waking aboard an expedition yacht, stepping outside with a cup of coffee as the morning mist lifts from a quiet Pacific Northwest anchorage.</p>
      <p>Breakfast is waiting. Your bike is ready. And today's trail system is somewhere completely different from the one you rode yesterday.</p>
      <p>Welcome to Ride the Salish Sea, a five day, four night mountain bike expedition unlike any cycling trip you've taken before. We travel aboard Supernova from Washington's San Juan Islands into British Columbia, using the yacht as our floating lodge and our landing craft to carry riders and bikes straight from the water to shore.</p>
      <p>By day, ride some of the Pacific Northwest's most memorable forests and trail systems. By night, come back to a hot shower in your private stateroom, a chef prepared Northwest dinner, a comfortable bed and another beautiful anchorage.</p>
      <p><strong>No hotels. No ferry schedules. No packing and unpacking.</strong> Just ride, eat, recover, explore and wake up somewhere new.</p>

      <h2>This isn't a normal bike tour</h2>
      <p>A typical destination cycling trip goes: ride, pack, drive, check in, unpack, repeat.</p>
      <p>We've replaced all of that with: <strong>ride, board, shower, eat, relax, sleep, wake up at tomorrow's trailhead.</strong></p>
      <p>With a small group aboard, we build each day's riding around the people on the boat.</p>
    </div>
