<section id="itinerary" style="scroll-margin-top:100px">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:860px">
    <span class="eyebrow">Sample itinerary</span>
    <h2>Five days in the Salish Sea</h2>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="day">
        <span class="tag">Day 1 · Anacortes → Orcas Island → Stuart Island</span>
        <h3>Moran State Park</h3>
        <p>Board Supernova early in Anacortes, settle into your stateroom and have breakfast as we cruise toward Orcas Island. After anchoring, the landing craft takes riders and bikes ashore for our first ride through the forests, lakes and mountain terrain of Moran State Park.</p>
        <p>Then back aboard: bike shoes off, hot showers, drinks and appetizers while we get underway for Stuart Island and dinner at anchor as the sun goes down.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="day">
        <span class="tag">Day 2 · Stuart Island → Canada → Tod Inlet</span>
        <h3>Hartland & Mount Work</h3>
        <p>Cross into Canada, clear entry and cruise to Tod Inlet near The Butchart Gardens. The landing craft puts us ashore for the Hartland and Mount Work trail system: towering evergreens, mossy rock, roots and rolling singletrack.</p>
        <p>Want more? Keep riding. Want to call it a day? Supernova is waiting. In the evening, walk The Butchart Gardens when operating hours permit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="day">
        <span class="tag">Day 3 · Tod Inlet → Maple Bay</span>
        <h3>Mount Tzouhalem</h3>
        <p>Breakfast underway as we head north to Maple Bay, home for two nights. Mount Tzouhalem is one of the Cowichan Valley's best known riding areas, with forested climbs, flowing singletrack and technical descents.</p>
        <p>When you're done there's no hotel shuttle. There's a boat. Hot shower, clean clothes, cold drink, fresh Northwest food.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="day">
        <span class="tag">Day 4 · Maple Bay</span>
        <h3>Maple Mountain</h3>
        <p>Wake up slowly, coffee on deck. Today we ride Maple Mountain, rising right beside the bay with purpose built trails, natural terrain and big coastal views. Push for a big day or shorten the ride and enjoy the yacht.</p>
        <p>The final night brings a farewell dinner aboard: think wild salmon, Dungeness crab when available, seasonal vegetables and Northwest flavors.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="day">
        <span class="tag">Day 5 · Maple Bay → Anacortes</span>
        <h3>The voyage home</h3>
        <p>Breakfast as we cruise south through the islands, watching for seals, porpoises and eagles. Clear U.S. entry and arrive back in Anacortes with five days of riding behind you.</p>
        <p><strong>Your bags moved once. Your hotel moved every day.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Itinerary and riding locations may change due to weather, trail conditions, seasonal trail restrictions, customs requirements and other operational needs. Wildlife sightings cannot be guaranteed.</p>
  </div>
</section>

